kes the it makes the trade deal  look i think the president's word were  uh  it seems much less of a priority for me  today notwithstanding that we hope that  the  first part of the phase one trade deal  is complied with uh we hope there are  places that we can work  with china we want good things for the  chinese people  what we're never going to sacrifice is  american national security and  american economic prosperity so i hope  that the  chinese will decide that their  commitments under the phase one trade  deal  must be complied with we they tell us  that they will uh we'll wait  and see if they come through with their  obligations there that's it reminds me  of  an old line from ronald reagan that he  would quote to uh mikhail gorbachev  trust but verify and i i certainly it  would seem apt for the relationship with  china  you know moving uh michael in my speech  last week michael i  i used that phrase and then described uh  how we should respond to the chinese  communist party as distrust but verify  that's right you know you've got to send  these standards they've broken they've  broken so many prompts michael they've  broken so many promises to  uh to the world they promised they  wouldn't arm the south china sea they  promised the people of hong kong they'd  have their freedom for 50 years  uh the list that they promised the world  health organization that they would fess  up if they had a problem  um this is what happens in authoritarian  regimes  and and you're seeing the effect of that  too i mean i remember early on in the  pandemic there was a study came out of  university of southampton  that said if china had just stopped  lying about the virus  one week earlier it would have reduced  transmission possibly by 66 percent  two weeks earlier 86 percent three weeks  earlier over  90 percent and i think a lot of people  are  are hoping that there will be some  consequence to be paid  or or at least a more just view of our  relationship  moving into the 